    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στάγῑρος</span></b> , ἡ, a city
		in Chalcidice, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			7.115
		</span></i>, etc.; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στάγιρα</span></b> ,
			τά, <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			669
		</span></i>, etc.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σταγιρίτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑτ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a Stagirite,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.195.27
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; esp. of Aristotle, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				275
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), St. Byz.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σταγιρόθεν</span></b> , <i>from
			Stagira</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tz.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				4.131
			</span></i>. (In codd. usu. misspelt <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σταγειρ-</span></b> ).</div>
